d 'SLIDEGRAPH': module to automate stepped and layered graphs for presentation slides
d
d     slidegraph automates the creation of layered, stepped
d sequence graphs for  presentation slides (such as LaTeX Beamer or
d PowerPoint builds). Instead of  omitting series across sequential
d slides (which causes axis bounds, tick  intervals, margins, and
d legend bounding boxes to jump between frames),  slidegraph plots
d all series in every frame and modulates visibility using  Stata
d opacity modifiers (%0, %20, etc.). It supports binary revelation,
d  3-state narrative spotlighting (focus, dimmed ghost context, and
d off),  automated export to LaTeX Beamer overlay code, and dual
d paper/slide output  from a single command. 
d
d KW: graphics
d KW: sequence graphs
d KW: presentation slides
d
d Requires: Stata version 15
d
d Distribution-Date: 20261107
d
d Author:   Aaron Wolf,   Northwestern University
d Support: email  aaron.wolf@@u.northwestern.edu
d
f slidegraph.ado
f slidegraph.sthlp
f slidegraph_demo.do
